      "narrative": "Pima County\u2019s residential market in mid-2026 is characterized by steady demand, limited inventory, and mostly stable pricing, with median list prices holding rather than surging.[1][5] Inventory remains relatively tight and days on market are elevated, indicating that buyers have more time to choose but not an excess of homes; one recent local snapshot cited 283 active homes and an average 74 days on market alongside a median rent of $2,138 per month.[5] This balance has produced a more cautious, negotiated environment, where sellers cannot assume rapid, above-list sales but buyers are not yet in a deeply discounted, oversupplied market.[1][3] Local dynamics are influenced by broader Tucson-area employers and ongoing housing-affordability discussions, reflected in the county\u2019s Regional Affordable Housing Commission work on gap analyses and policy responses.[7]",
